course: dictionary
lesson: 13856
title: Jubilee: a special anniversary
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A jubilee is a special anniversary, a day or year when people celebrate how long something has lasted. The words around it are clues. «The town held a jubilee street party with bunting, music and cake.» Street parties, bunting and cake show that a jubilee is a big celebration.
explain: Numbers can be clues too. «The queen's golden jubilee was a celebration of 50 years.» Golden means 50 here, so a jubilee names how many years are being celebrated. Silver is 25, diamond is 60 and platinum is 70.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The school's jubilee was a great day for everyone.» If you put "a great celebration" in place of jubilee, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A jubilee is a special anniversary, when people celebrate a number of years.
fact: Royal jubilees: silver is 25 years, golden is 50, diamond is 60 and platinum is 70.
fact: A jubilee can also mean a time of great celebration and joy, as in «a jubilee street party».
fact: In the Old Testament, a jubilee came every fiftieth year: slaves were set free, debts were cancelled and land was returned.
fact: In the Catholic Church, a jubilee is a special holy year of pilgrimage and forgiveness.
exercise: «The town held a jubilee street party with bunting and cake.» What is a jubilee here? | *A big celebration | A long walk in the hills | A type of cake | A quiet day for sleeping
exercise: The queen's golden jubilee is how many years? | *50 | 25 | 60 | 70
exercise: «The family planned a diamond jubilee for Grandma.» How many years is a diamond jubilee? | *60 | 70 | 25 | 50
test: Which jubilee celebrates 70 years? | Golden | *Platinum | Diamond | Silver
test: «The school had a jubilee to celebrate its anniversary.» What is a school jubilee? | A school exam | A sports match | A lost bag | *An anniversary celebration
exam: Which statement is true? | A golden jubilee is 25 years | A diamond jubilee is 50 years | *A golden jubilee is 50 years | A platinum jubilee is 60 years
